    {
      "id": "docs_adr_readme_filing_convention",
      "label": "ADR filing convention",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/adr/README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Filename NNNN-short-kebab-slug.md, next available number wins. Required sections: Context, Decision, Consequences, Alternatives, Status (Proposed/Accepted/Superseded by NNNN/Deprecated), Date. ADRs 0001\u20130003 are a deliberate one-time exception to the no-historical-backfill guidance, for discoverability in a showcase repo; 0004 onward follow the guidance."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_adr_readme_superseding",
      "label": "ADR superseding policy",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/adr/README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "A superseded ADR is kept in place for historical continuity; the newer ADR names the superseded number and the old record's Status becomes 'Superseded by NNNN'. History is annotated, never deleted or reused."
    }
